>>
endobj
417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1162 0 R
/E (In reality, longer lead times tend to co-occur with higher ADR \(advance bookings often lock in different pricing tiers\) and specific deposit types \(non-refundable deposits are frequently tied to early, discounted bookings\). This violates NB's core assumption and limits its ability to model how these factors jointly influence cancellation risk.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1163 0 R
/E (Random Forest , on the other hand , doesn't require feature independence and can capture interaction effects . )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
